# Backend (Node.js + TypeScript + TypeORM)

- Every route goes through centralized authn/authz unless explicitly public in the typed route registry.
- Controllers are thin: request/response mapping and error forwarding only. No business logic, DB queries, or Keycloak calls in controllers.
- Business rules live in services/use cases; they receive typed inputs and an `AuthContext` when authorization-relevant.
- Validate every body, query, params, and header contract at runtime.
- Use migrations; never `synchronize: true` in production. Parameterize queries, avoid N+1, paginate lists.
- Do not return raw TypeORM entities from APIs; map to DTOs.
- Use typed errors mapped to a consistent API error envelope. Never leak stack traces or ORM errors.

For deeper guidance load:
`resources/backend-node-typeorm.md`, `resources/auth-keycloak-rbac.md`,
`resources/database-typeorm-data-access.md`, `resources/api-contracts-and-errors.md`.
